# =============================================================================
# Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8 — dual DGX Spark TP=2 (PRODUCTION-QUALIFIED, c1/c2)
#
# Status:              PRODUCTION-QUALIFIED -- Gate0-2 and Gate3(c1) PASSED
#                      (2026-08-29, MAX_NUM_SEQS=1); Gate3 c2/c4 at
#                      MAX_NUM_SEQS=4 (unbounded) remains BLOCKED -- see the
#                      "Runtime contract" and "MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 CUDA-graph
#                      production requalification" blocks below for the
#                      distinct, bounded MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 recipe that IS
#                      qualified for production. This preset's server-side
#                      concurrency cap is MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 -- c4/c8 client load
#                      is accepted and queued, not rejected, but only c1/c2
#                      have themselves been measured; treat c4/c8 as queue
#                      pressure on a 2-slot server, not as a separately
#                      qualified concurrency level.
#                      See docs/qwen3.8-flash-next-tp2.md for the full gate
#                      ledger, exact evidence paths, and client guidance on
#                      thinking mode.
# Current state:       Bounded c2 Gate PASSED, followed by a full 12-row/135-
#                      request llama-benchy suite (12/12 rows, 135/135
#                      requests, c8 protocol/syntax/semantic 8/8, 0 errors/
#                      fatals) and a successful 4-hour c1/c2 soak (target
#                      14400s, actual 14400.0001s; 1120/1120 records --
#                      640 model requests + 480 health checks; post-c1 and
#                      post-c2 gates both PASS; 0 fatal/restart/OOM events)
#                      on spark01/spark02 (2026-08-31 -> 2026-09-01). Both
#                      nodes stopped/cleaned up after every run, nothing left
#                      running. This preset defines a validated PRODUCTION
#                      runtime config -- it is NOT an auto-start service; a
#                      launch still requires the worker-first procedure in
#                      docs/qwen3.8-flash-next-tp2.md §6.
# Role:                Production CUDA-graph envelope at MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 with
#                      FULL_DECODE_ONLY capture sizes [1,2]. Do not raise
#                      MAX_NUM_SEQS above 2 or add capture sizes beyond [1,2]
#                      without separately re-qualifying at the target value
#                      first -- MAX_NUM_SEQS=4 unbounded concurrency remains
#                      BLOCKED per the 2026-08-29 ledger (see below).
#
# Follow-up (2026-08-29, docs/qwen3.8-flash-next-tp2.md §5.6): a narrower
# single-variable diagnostic series at MAX_MODEL_LEN=32768 / MAX_NUM_SEQS=2
# found exact-output fixed-byte payloads deterministic at c1 and c2, while
# open-ended code generation still diverged at c2 (prefix caching on/off and
# expert-parallel off were each excluded as the cause; a CUTLASS FP8 MoE
# backend trial failed before readiness). This 32K/c2 result did not by
# itself requalify MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 at this preset's MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144
# default -- the actual MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 production requalification below is a
# separate, later, bounded-CUDA-graph runtime result (2026-08-31/09-01), not
# a promotion of this 32K/c2 follow-up.
#
# MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 CUDA-graph production requalification (2026-08-31 ->
# 2026-09-01, distinct from and later than the 32K/c2 follow-up above):
# bounded c2 Gate PASS, then a full 12-row/135-request llama-benchy suite
# (12/12 rows, 135/135 requests, c8 protocol/syntax/semantic 8/8, 0 errors/
# fatals) at /home/bjk110/docker-build/qwen38-graphonly-c2-capture12-fullbench-k1031-20260831/,
# then a 4-hour c1/c2 soak (target 14400s, actual 14400.0001s; 1120/1120
# records -- 640 model requests + 480 health checks; post-c1 and post-c2
# gates both PASS; 0 fatal/restart/OOM events; this was a successful retry
# after an earlier attempt was archived for a writer-race condition, see
# that run's own archive/ subdirectory) at
# /home/bjk110/docker-build/qwen38-graphonly-c2-capture12-soak4h-k1031-20260901/
# (current top-level outputs). Both runs measured GB10 UMA MemAvailable
# minima of ~9.9 GB (spark01) / ~14.2 GB (spark02) mid-run; teardown left
# ~19 GB MemAvailable on both nodes -- per this repository's UMA-recovery
# lesson, reboot before the next fresh launch if that low-19GB state is
# still current. Server-side MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 means client concurrency above
# 2 is accepted and queued by vLLM, not rejected -- c4/c8 client load in the
# evidence above exercises queue pressure on this 2-slot server, not an
# independently qualified c4/c8 concurrency level.
#
# Model (official FP8 checkpoint, NOT BF16 -- BF16 is 335.28 GiB and does not fit
# safely on 2x121.63 GiB GB10 UMA):
#   Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8
#   HF revision (exact, pinned): 970c569adaca6b35532111fd6b27351b2baefe50
#   Weight bytes: 185523317458 (172.78 GiB)
#   See docs/qwen3.8-flash-next-tp2.md for the model-card/recipe citations,
#   checksum verification guidance, and the excluded-alternatives rationale
#   (BF16 full-precision and PLE-offloaded NVFP4 are both excluded here).
#
# Image (immutable, digest-pinned; official recipe states PyPI is unsupported for
# this model and requires vLLM >=0.28 / nightly -- this image is the dedicated,
# pre-built runtime that satisfies that requirement, NOT a general-purpose
# vllm-spark image):
#   vllm/vllm-openai:qwen38-flash-next@sha256:3b0e188ffceb3d07e09c3cb5215433a0020eacf02d7f882ed3a8bfd15454477e
#   arm64 manifest digest pinned above; the human-readable tag is informational
#   only -- Docker resolves and pulls by the digest, so a tag re-push upstream
#   cannot silently change what this preset launches.
#
# Runtime contract (production envelope; MAX_NUM_SEQS and the compilation
# config below are this cluster's own measured requalification -- see the
# "MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 CUDA-graph production requalification" block above -- every
# other value is unchanged from the original conservative envelope, which
# itself matched the known dual-Spark community command referenced in
# docs/qwen3.8-flash-next-tp2.md and was not independently tuned):
#   TP=2, one GPU/node, DISTRIBUTED_BACKEND=mp over 200 Gbps RoCE;
#   MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144 (native); MAX_NUM_SEQS=2; MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=8192;
#   GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.83; expert parallel enabled;
#   VLLM_ALL2ALL_BACKEND=allgather_reducescatter; chunked prefill enabled;
#   FlashInfer autotune disabled; qwen3 reasoning parser; qwen3_coder tool
#   parser; default (lazy/mmap) safetensors loading -- no --load-format override;
#   --compilation-config {"mode":0,"cudagraph_mode":"FULL_DECODE_ONLY","cudagraph_capture_sizes":[1,2]}
#   (torch.compile disabled via mode:0/NONE, CUDA-graph decode capture enabled
#   at exactly the two production concurrency levels -- see "CUDA-graph
#   requalification" item below for why this replaces --enforce-eager).
#
# Safety hardening (added prior to this candidate's FIRST runtime launch, per
# community evidence gathered after the preset above was drafted -- none of
# this reflects this cluster's own measurement, and each item is conservative
# by construction, matching this candidate's overall posture):
#   - CUDA-graph requalification (supersedes the original --enforce-eager
#     item below): a DGX Spark (GB10) community dual-Spark report
#     (x00byte/Qwen3.8-Flash-Dual-Spark-Recipe,
#     https://github.com/x00byte/Qwen3.8-Flash-Dual-Spark-Recipe) states that
#     removing --enforce-eager caused torch.compile/cudagraph startup to hang
#     and then exit 255, and left the GB10 host unresponsive; their own
#     known-good dual-Spark profile keeps --enforce-eager set. That report
#     motivated --enforce-eager as this candidate's first-launch default.
#     This cluster's own 2026-08-31 -> 2026-09-01 runtime evidence (see the
#     "MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 CUDA-graph production requalification" block above)
#     found that --compilation-config {"mode":0,"cudagraph_mode":
#     "FULL_DECODE_ONLY","cudagraph_capture_sizes":[1,2]} -- torch.compile
#     itself off (mode:0/NONE), CUDA-graph decode capture on for exactly
#     [1,2] -- passed the bounded c2 Gate, the full 12-row/135-request
#     llama-benchy suite, and the 4-hour c1/c2 soak with 0 fatal/restart/OOM
#     events, superseding --enforce-eager as this preset's production
#     default. This does not itself qualify a larger capture-size set or
#     torch.compile mode>0 -- do not extend cudagraph_capture_sizes or raise
#     mode without separately re-qualifying.
#   - MAX_JOBS=4 / FLASHINFER_NVCC_THREADS=1: bounds any FlashInfer JIT
#     compile that occurs at runtime to a small number of concurrent
#     nvcc/cicc processes, the same mechanism and rationale already
#     documented at docker-compose.yml's MAX_JOBS/FLASHINFER_NVCC_THREADS
#     passthrough comment (unbounded ninja parallelism can spike toward the
#     ~170 GiB GB10 UMA ceiling). Applied here pre-emptively for this
#     candidate's first launch rather than only after an observed problem.
#   - PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF explicitly empty: a current dual-Spark SGLang
#     recipe explicitly warns that PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True
#     is unproven on GB10 and is absent from known-good dual-Spark recipes.
#     This repository's base docker-compose.yml defaults
#     PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF to expandable_segments:True when the variable is
#     unset (see docker-compose.yml's
#     `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=${PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF:-expandable_segments:True}`).
#     For this candidate specifically, the required compose overlay
#     (compose/qwen3.8-flash-next/docker-compose.candidate.yml) now forces
#     PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF to an explicit empty value for BOTH the head and
#     worker services, so the base compose default cannot silently apply. This
#     preset does not set PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF at all (see the ---- Runtime
#     env ---- block below) -- the overlay is the enforcement point, not this
#     file, because Compose's `${VAR:-default}` substitution treats a
#     set-but-empty preset value the same as unset and would still apply the
#     base default; only the overlay's own `${PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF-}`
#     (unset-only fallback) reliably yields an empty rendered value.
#
# Explicitly OFF / NOT included in this conservative candidate:
#   - VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT: NOT set. 2026-08-29 static preflight (see
#     docs/qwen3.8-flash-next-tp2.md §5.7) found GDNAttentionBackend.supports_batch_invariance
#     resolves to the inherited AttentionBackend.supports_batch_invariance (always returns False)
#     in the pinned image (vLLM 0.1.dev20073+g8e685d198) -- unsupported for this GDN backend. Per
#     fail-closed policy the 32K/c2 runtime gate was deliberately not launched with this flag
#     (would be rejected with "VLLM batch_invariant mode is not supported for GDN_ATTN"); this is a
#     static classification, not an observed runtime failure. Do not set VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1
#     here without a separately authorized image change. Evidence:
#     /home/bjk110/docker-build/qwen38-fp8-bic-support-check-20260829/
#   - MTP speculative decoding: no --speculative-config. MTP is a separate,
#     explicitly experimental LATER profile (not this preset) -- see
#     docs/qwen3.8-flash-next-tp2.md "MTP (experimental, not default)". It is
#     gated on this conservative candidate first passing its own deterministic
#     correctness gate.
#   - PLE CPU offload: not used. See docs/qwen3.8-flash-next-tp2.md for the
#     vLLM issue #53960 PLE-offload deadlock citation that motivates this
#     exclusion.
#   - --language-model-only: NOT set. Full multimodal support is preserved
#     deliberately -- do not add this flag to this preset.
#   - --load-format override: NOT set. vLLM's default ("auto") already resolves
#     to the lazy/mmap-backed safetensors_weights_iterator branch for a
#     safetensors checkpoint (same default behavior documented for the
#     Solar-Open2 loader in this repo); an explicit lazy-loader flag is not a
#     real vLLM CLI option and is therefore not fabricated here.
#
# Compose overlay REQUIRED (adds the head healthcheck and the
# VLLM_ALL2ALL_BACKEND passthrough that base docker-compose.yml does not carry):
#   compose/qwen3.8-flash-next/docker-compose.candidate.yml
#
# Static verification (identities + safety contract, no containers started):
#   python3 scripts/diag/verify_qwen38_flash_next_recipe.py
#
# Full staged-gate procedure (Gate0-Gate3), model download/sync with checksum
# guidance, and known limitations: docs/qwen3.8-flash-next-tp2.md
# =============================================================================

# ---- Image ----
VLLM_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:qwen38-flash-next@sha256:3b0e188ffceb3d07e09c3cb5215433a0020eacf02d7f882ed3a8bfd15454477e
ENTRYPOINT_FILE=./entrypoints/entrypoint.sh

# ---- Model ----
MODEL_PATH=/home/bjk110/Documents/Models/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8
MODEL_CONTAINER_PATH=/models/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8

# ---- Cluster topology ----
CLUSTER_MODE=dual-rdma
TP_SIZE=2
HEAD_ROCE_IP=10.10.10.1
WORKER_ROCE_IP=10.10.10.2
ROCE_IF_NAME=enp1s0f0np0
IB_HCA_NAME=rocep1s0f0
RAY_PORT=6379          # unused in mp backend; kept for quick switch back to ray
DISTRIBUTED_BACKEND=mp
MASTER_PORT=50000

# ---- vLLM Serving (production envelope: MAX_NUM_SEQS=2 + CUDA-graph capture
# [1,2] are this cluster's own measured requalification; MAX_MODEL_LEN,
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION, and MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS are unchanged from the
# original conservative envelope and were not independently tuned) ----
HOST_PORT=8000
MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144
MAX_NUM_SEQS=2
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.83
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=8192

# ---- Extra args ----
# --enable-expert-parallel      : distribute MoE experts across TP ranks (matches
#                                  the conservative envelope; see docs for exact
#                                  expert count once measured).
# --no-enable-flashinfer-autotune: skip FlashInfer's JIT autotuning pass. Conservative
#                                  choice for a first bring-up -- avoids autotune-time
#                                  cost/variance while correctness is unproven; matches
#                                  the same flag used by the Step-3.7 presets in this repo.
# --enable-chunked-prefill      : reduce TTFT under concurrency (matches the
#                                  conservative envelope).
# --reasoning-parser qwen3       : parse <think>...</think> as reasoning_content.
# --enable-auto-tool-choice / --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder : tool-call parsing
#                                  for the Qwen3-Coder-style tool-call format.
# --compilation-config {"mode":0,"cudagraph_mode":"FULL_DECODE_ONLY",
#                       "cudagraph_capture_sizes":[1,2]} : torch.compile off
#                                  (mode:0/NONE), CUDA-graph decode capture on
#                                  at exactly the production concurrency
#                                  levels [1,2]. Replaces --enforce-eager
#                                  (which fully disabled torch.compile AND
#                                  cudagraph capture) per this cluster's own
#                                  2026-08-31 -> 2026-09-01 measured
#                                  requalification -- bounded c2 Gate PASS,
#                                  full 12-row/135-request llama-benchy suite,
#                                  and a 4-hour c1/c2 soak with 0 fatal/
#                                  restart/OOM events. See "Safety hardening"
#                                  block in the header above for the full
#                                  evidence paths and the original
#                                  --enforce-eager community citation this
#                                  supersedes.
#
# Deliberately absent: --speculative-config (MTP off), --language-model-only
# (multimodal preserved), --load-format (default lazy safetensors), any
# CPU-offload flag (PLE offload excluded), --enforce-eager (superseded by
# --compilation-config above). See header block above.
#
# --compilation-config above takes a JSON-valued argument, so the single-argv-
# token quoting concern noted elsewhere in this repo applies here: VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS
# is space-split by entrypoint.sh (see entrypoints/entrypoint.sh), so the JSON
# above is kept compact with NO internal spaces, exactly as every other
# JSON-bearing VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS in presets/ does (e.g.
# {"method":"deepseek_mtp","num_speculative_tokens":1}) -- Compose env-file
# syntax strips surrounding quotes, so quoting cannot be relied on to keep a
# JSON blob a single token.
VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS=--enable-expert-parallel --no-enable-flashinfer-autotune --enable-chunked-prefill --reasoning-parser qwen3 --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser qwen3_coder --compilation-config {"mode":0,"cudagraph_mode":"FULL_DECODE_ONLY","cudagraph_capture_sizes":[1,2]}

# ---- Multi-node all-to-all backend (MoE expert-parallel collective path) ----
# allgather_reducescatter is the conservative envelope's choice. Not in
# base docker-compose.yml's environment list -- forwarded by the required
# compose/qwen3.8-flash-next/docker-compose.candidate.yml overlay.
VLLM_ALL2ALL_BACKEND=allgather_reducescatter

# ---- Runtime env ----
# PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF deliberately NOT set here. This preset relies on
# compose/qwen3.8-flash-next/docker-compose.candidate.yml to force an explicit
# empty value for BOTH head and worker -- see the "Safety hardening" block in
# the header above for why setting it here (even to an empty string) is not
# sufficient on its own to prevent base docker-compose.yml's
# `${PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF:-expandable_segments:True}` default from applying.
NCCL_IB_DISABLE=0
NCCL_DEBUG=WARN
# NVLS is meaningless on NVLink-less RoCE-only DGX Spark pairs; see .env.example.
NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE=0
NCCL_NET=
VLLM_USE_BREAKABLE_CUDAGRAPH=0
VLLM_MEMORY_PROFILER_ESTIMATE_CUDAGRAPHS=1
FLASHINFER_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=12.1
# Bound FlashInfer JIT compile parallelism (see "Safety hardening" block in
# the header above and docker-compose.yml's own MAX_JOBS/FLASHINFER_NVCC_THREADS
# passthrough comment for the GB10 UMA rationale).
MAX_JOBS=4
FLASHINFER_NVCC_THREADS=1
# No-op under DISTRIBUTED_BACKEND=mp (Ray-specific); left set for parity with
# every other dual-rdma preset in this repo, harmless either way.
VLLM_USE_RAY_V2_EXECUTOR_BACKEND=0
# VLLM_NCCL_SO_PATH deliberately unset: the pinned image lacks this path, and
# docker-compose.yml already puts the pip NCCL directory on LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
